After having a long run of bad games, I finally seem to be starting a 
good one. Found a wand of polymorph early on, so my Priest got some 
good weapons and armor near the start.

I had three unidentified rings.  Since I was a Priest I knew they weren't
cursed, so I tried them on (hoping for a ring of conflict).  One turned
out to be searching.  The second I couldn't figure out.  I tried on the
third, and continued playing.

Using telepathy on level 6 or so, I noticed another @ on the right
side on the screen (I was hoping it was a shopkeeper).  I started to
make my way over there, when I turn into a cockatrice - now I know
what that third ring is.

All my armor and weapons falls off me.  I can't carry much, so I just
hang onto my Excaliber so that if I change back I won't be defenseless.
Now Peter the cockatrice wanders over to the shop...

This was my first good game in a long while.  Should I try to kill the
shopkeeper, or should I just wait to turn back to human and use some other 
method to rob the shop?

I decide to try to kill the shopkeeper.  I figure I'd better turn him to
stone on my first hit, or he'll probably kill me.  I attack:

You miss the shopkeeper [I forget his name] -- more -- 
[arrrrgh]
























The shopkeeper hits -- The shopkeeper misses -- more --
[arrrrrrrgh]






















The shopkeeper hits! -- The shopkeeper turns to stone!

Amazing!  I never knew that the cockatrice's stoning ability was defensive!
I now claimed the shop, all the shopkeepers gold, etc.
For the next few minutes, until I changed back to human, I sat on top on
my pile of armor, waiting to be able to put it on.  Monsters kept coming up 
to me, hitting me, and turing to stone.  I finally turned back to human, 
got all my armor back on, and saved the game (I had to leave).

Hopefully the rest of this game will go as well.

